      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thomas Flury and Neil Shephard (University of Oxford)",
      "bbox": [
        48.08985900878906,
        229.71653747558594,
        257.4346618652344,
        238.02838134765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We congratulate Christophe Andrieu, Arnaud Doucet and Roman Holenstein for this important contri-",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        239.67909240722656,
        443.607666015625,
        247.99093627929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bution to the sequential Monte Carlo and Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) literature. At the base of",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        249.6416473388672,
        443.605712890625,
        257.9534912109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "their paper is the deceivingly simple looking idea of combining two powerful and well-known Monte Carlo",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        259.60418701171875,
        443.607666015625,
        267.9160461425781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithms to create a truly Herculean tool for statisticians. They use sequential Monte Carlo methods to",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        269.5667419433594,
        443.612060546875,
        277.87860107421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "generate high dimensional proposal distributions for MCMC algorithms.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        279.529296875,
        324.8027648925781,
        287.8411560058594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We focus our discussion on one very speciﬁc insight: one can use an unbiased simulation-based estimator",
      "bbox": [
        57.05712890625,
        289.4918518066406,
        443.612060546875,
        297.8037109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the likelihood inside an MCMC algorithm to perform Bayesian inference. For dynamic models this esti-",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        299.45440673828125,
        443.60302734375,
        307.7662658691406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mator is obtained from a standard particle ﬁlter. Importantly, this means that the particle ﬁlter now offers",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        309.4169616699219,
        443.6128845214844,
        317.72882080078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a complete extension of the Kalman ﬁlter: it can carry out ﬁltering and now direct parameter estimation.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        319.3795166015625,
        443.6138610839844,
        327.6913757324219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We are particularly impressed with the minimalistic assumptions that we need to perform likelihood-",
      "bbox": [
        57.05712890625,
        329.3420715332031,
        443.6050109863281,
        337.6539306640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "based inference in dynamic non-linear and non-Gaussian state space models, which is of great interest for",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        339.30462646484375,
        443.6119079589844,
        347.6164855957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "microeconometrics, macroeconometrics and ﬁnancial econometrics. In the particle marginal Metropolis–",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        349.2671813964844,
        443.60748291015625,
        357.57904052734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hastings algorithm we only need to be able to evaluate the measurement density and to sample from the",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        359.229736328125,
        443.610107421875,
        367.5415954589844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state transition density. Another advantage is that we do not need an inﬁnite number of simulation draws",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        369.1922912597656,
        443.6131286621094,
        377.504150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for consistency: all theoretical results hold from as little as N ⩾1 particles. Practical implementation is",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        378.40167236328125,
        443.6068115234375,
        387.4667053222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "also very easy as one only needs to change very few lines of code to estimate a different model.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        389.1174011230469,
        405.0251159667969,
        397.42926025390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Flury and Shephard (2010) we showed the power of this method on four famous examples in econo-",
      "bbox": [
        57.05712890625,
        399.0799560546875,
        443.6112976074219,
        407.3918151855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "metrics. Other applications, such as in repeated auctions, will also become important. Our experience",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        409.0425109863281,
        443.606689453125,
        417.3543701171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is that these methods work, are quite simple to implement, general purpose and highly computationally",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        419.00506591796875,
        443.60772705078125,
        427.3169250488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "demanding. The last point is important; they take so long to run that it is tempting to use the phrase",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        428.9676208496094,
        443.61102294921875,
        437.27947998046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "‘computationally brutal’.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        438.9302062988281,
        143.44842529296875,
        447.2420654296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Christian P. Robert and Pierre Jacob (Centre de Recherche en Economie et Statistique and Université",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        458.8553161621094,
        422.5876159667969,
        467.16717529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Paris Dauphine, Paris), Nicolas Chopin (Ecole Nationale de la Statistique et de l’Administration",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        468.8179016113281,
        403.67755126953125,
        477.1297607421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Economique, Paris) and Håvard Rue (Norwegian University for Science and Technology, Trondheim)",
      "bbox": [
        48.090728759765625,
        478.78045654296875,
        420.71099853515625,
        487.0923156738281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We congratulate the authors for opening a new vista for running Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC)",
      "bbox": [
        48.09161376953125,
        488.7430114746094,
        443.6083984375,
        497.05487060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithms in state space models. Being able to devise a correct Markovian scheme based on a particle",
      "bbox": [
        48.09161376953125,
        498.7055969238281,
        443.6102294921875,
        507.0174560546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximation of the target distribution is a genuine tour de force that deserves enthusiastic recognition!",
      "bbox": [
        48.09161376953125,
        508.6681823730469,
        443.606689453125,
        516.9800415039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "This is all the more impressive when considering that the ratio",
      "bbox": [
        48.09161376953125,
        518.6307373046875,
        282.4821472167969,
        526.9425659179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ˆpθ.xÅ",
      "bbox": [
        185.1340789794922,
        529.2366333007812,
        206.48089599609375,
        542.4052734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T |y1:T /= ˆpθ{x1:T .i−1/|y1:T }",
      "bbox": [
        201.9615936279297,
        531.8817749023438,
        306.56463623046875,
        543.2601928710938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".54/",
      "bbox": [
        427.89794921875,
        532.6349487304688,
        443.6070861816406,
        540.94677734375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is not unbiased and thus invalidates the usual importance sampling solutions, as demonstrated by Beau-",
      "bbox": [
        48.089324951171875,
        548.6292114257812,
        443.6116638183594,
        556.9410400390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "mont et al. (2009). Thus, the resolution of simulating by conditioning on the lineage truly is an awesome",
      "bbox": [
        48.089324951171875,
        558.591796875,
        443.60992431640625,
        566.9036254882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "resolution of the problem!",
      "bbox": [
        48.08842468261719,
        568.5543823242188,
        147.1313018798828,
        576.8662109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We implemented the particle Hastings–Metropolis algorithm for the (notoriously challenging) stochastic",
      "bbox": [
        57.05482482910156,
        578.5169677734375,
        443.6053466796875,
        586.8287963867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "volatility model",
      "bbox": [
        48.08842468261719,
        588.4794921875,
        107.81361389160156,
        596.7913208007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "yt|xt ∼N{0, exp.xt/},",
      "bbox": [
        136.9320068359375,
        602.7239990234375,
        219.9644317626953,
        613.0353393554688
      ],
      "direction": [
